# Code quality

## Formatting

- Follow Prettier: 2-space indent, single quotes, no semicolons, trailing commas.
- Do not mix 4-space indent or optional semicolons in touched files.

## Comments (English only)

- Comments only where code is not self-explanatory (non-trivial logic, business rule, API constraint).
- No obvious comments. No “changed here” notes — that belongs in the PR/commit.
- TODOs only with a ticket: `// TODO [ISSUE-ID]: short description`.

## Cleanliness

- Do not commit `console.log`, debug leftovers, commented-out “for later” code, unused imports/variables.
- Do not duplicate logic: check `src/hooks/`, `src/utils/`, `src/components/`, `src/ui/` and reuse.
- Prefer existing UI: Ant Design, or `src/ui/Button` for the custom variants. Do not add a second button kit.

## Tests

- Match neighboring style (`describe` / `it`, matchers, mocks).
- Place `*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx` next to the code under test. No `__tests__/` unless that area already uses them.

## AI agent artifacts

- Scratch files only under `ailocal/` (gitignored). Do not scatter temp files under `src/`.

## README

- Feature setup (secret, env, tool, MCP) goes in `README.md` only.
